  "structure": {
    "block_count": 45,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "'Lightning Crotch' During Pregnancy Is Uncomfortable — Here's How to Deal With It",
        "text_sha256": "f807a76f19f26d330113a6d70b37c4eaad9b98f0ffcef845ecf45a84110becd2",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Light copy updates, updates to sourcing, and fact-checked for accuracy.",
        "text_sha256": "ce4b0fa95b50aecf6e7b67e3e57fba87415f35177add6e78e3c831eddc829533",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Bright yellow lightning bolt on a pastel gradient background",
        "text_sha256": "8a1e10091c4cf534cae225dd4f3f171456dc000b120291245b33bebdae0aee20",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A punched-in-the-crotch sensation when you’re expecting isn’t unusual, but it is uncomfortable. Happily, it’s not something to worry about.",
        "text_sha256": "eebfdb8c7f054183b928fa94178a37848a2a53a2bddd6db3f82e8cee43197c53",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Have you been struck by lightning crotch? There’s no medical term for super painful vaginal or pelvic electric-bolt twinges during pregnancy, but plenty of moms-to-be experience what’s been dubbed \"lightning crotch\" toward the end of their pregnancies.",
        "text_sha256": "ae1eee58b149d4d80ef2a0ab9015fda7918ff03239036dab96ce758de403b4a5",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"To me, [lightning crotch] feels like a needle being stabbed into my nether regions, very short and sharp,\" says What to Expect Community user SailyBay. \"If it’s bad, it stops me in my tracks. No rhyme or reason to it!\"",
        "text_sha256": "62d4a2ac0bbe85f16fd3725840e0a004e70acbafb4f3a2188d4ab538eefda8ff",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The good news is that it isn’t dangerous, nor is it a sign that there’s a problem.",
        "text_sha256": "6d6be130ace240b53c76061e823f5290c320698f55a913e5d9a003d8b2381c68",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Lightning crotch is a sharp, sudden, electric-like pain in the pelvic or vaginal area that many women experience late in pregnancy, often lasting only a few seconds and caused by nerve pressure or the baby’s position.",
        "text_sha256": "2d30c160be79a05a55f45bc416a46eb83cb7b34b5a5f339cbb696b4b33e29b74",
        "word_count": 36
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It’s harmless but uncomfortable, and while there’s no real way to prevent it, changing positions or wearing a belly support band may offer brief relief.",
        "text_sha256": "c3d0c441b18a73acf7c779bf851851220a5e3ca9b3c632e149f25ed574c7dce0",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Call your doctor if the pain lasts longer than a few seconds or is accompanied by bleeding, fever, or contractions, as those can signal a more serious issue.",
        "text_sha256": "af81a3ee8118cc1fa8fc71659f313e48f6876dd5164612201710a8ec6fea6a42",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What is \"lightning crotch\" during pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "16962b23604f4bff041cdc94f225a710f367660d512d7fd7d42a5c73fe2db6b5",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Have you ever experienced a sudden, sharp pain deep inside your crotch? Something that feels like a strong jab, perhaps, or an electric shock, maybe with some burning, pins and needles, or stinging thrown in?",
        "text_sha256": "1a8014f0e2fb1e35682d89303e31744a5702f8812249e6e367449a40ac0823b9",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If the answer is yes, then you’ve experienced what's known as lightning crotch. The very uncomfortable, take-your-breath-away deep pelvic pain is surprisingly common during late pregnancy, and it typically hits without any warning at all. Trusted SourceCleveland ClinicPregnancy DiscomfortsSee All Sources [1]",
        "text_sha256": "fe91609da3d61c321042575ea01741b6c260f006330d015ac046b60ed03f288e",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Pregnancy Discomforts",
        "text_sha256": "844b969ff4014cfb54aad25fe1636f33272d05649cdd7d3033454047fff4bb31",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Keep in mind that the pain from lightning crotch should last just a few seconds. Anything longer warrants bringing it up with your practitioner, as it could signal something more serious.",
        "text_sha256": "e7276ebbe11b68228ec7320fb2630bdc4594853980103408c95a02afc1206bdc",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Symptoms of lightning crotch",
        "text_sha256": "3488dbb7aba8db073427ccd62979bcdd5d6fd2d2a46926f63c5e518e24405b93",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Lightning crotch can feel a little different from person to person, but most often this pregnancy symptom manifests as:",
        "text_sha256": "1810bf24f73c76b8903230b22ec63f68bde81bc259945760b2b6ae0f6911907a",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Sharp, shooting pain in the vagina or pelvic area that lasts only for a moment",
        "text_sha256": "923c9587010dc55534b98f1fc39cad4262c25616e878950b4bc65ef6bbbc78cd",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Stinging or a pins-and-needles sensation in the same region",
        "text_sha256": "7e0ad0c3d0f0d0e375b5e1fe7dba045264fb63d0afd6ec71dc3b4763e9d55ff9",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Brief but intense pelvic pain that's stronger and shorter than menstrual cramps",
        "text_sha256": "205af9b2e3052f0cd2012b06f64a3e9e52c9e45efeed6a4194a147094834cfc2",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What can you do for relief?",
        "text_sha256": "fc4e4690e045b651caef82314485410572538832857809ab5279039ee6aef7b0",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here’s the real deal about lightning crotch — and it’s probably not something you want to hear: There’s not much you can do when it strikes, other than grin and bear it (or yelp loudly in pain). There are a couple of things you can try for relief, however: Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsChronic Pelvic PainSee All Sources [2]",
        "text_sha256": "bd75da138c53fb1e929304862dc5a8de16d57abe62772bfe64c933055da39a7b",
        "word_count": 61
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsChronic Pelvic PainSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "7fb8cf59ab2c851148fcab53e614328588d81b758ff71539c352bdc1c2aa4272",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Change positions in an effort to get baby off your nerves (literally) — so stand up if you’re lying down or sitting, or sit down if you’ve been standing.",
        "text_sha256": "f341f3c63108918763fcdcaeb87d16e1e1cbe4802803fafd55aaaad50aedeae8",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Wear a belly support garment or belt to help lighten the load on your pelvis.",
        "text_sha256": "9392164ad4d7523e780f106761014057071ddbc38741fded1178e1ac20a5863e",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Don’t be shocked if nothing seems to work though. Lightning crotch may be one of those pregnancy symptoms you just have to deal with.",
        "text_sha256": "7dc68822076b0522f560f29e46c6b8e738cd93911ebd75263441d657712fcd95",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What's the difference between lightning crotch pain and other pelvic pain during pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "3c0f770500d6898557f036c98b41c0a23dc03882a191154ad1f9b2674b2d9843",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There are plenty of aches and pains you’ll feel during pregnancy, especially in the pelvic area where so much of the action is happening. General pelvic pain or discomfort is common , but it's more of an achy, crampy feeling than a sudden shooting sensation like lightning crotch is.",
        "text_sha256": "30c01f62d9c2e4ac17bec0912cd6372777219e8cf9f30027d46d4bc0382a493f",
        "word_count": 49
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There’s also round ligament pain , often described as a pulling sensation in your lower abdomen and pelvic area. Then there’s sciatica , pain in the pelvic and rectum area that usually radiates down the leg. Or you might experience painful pressure down there coming from varicose veins in the vulva.",
        "text_sha256": "2dbb0d59b0c0f89149faf5f39261695982940f9b3f0153021ce94718646865e8",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "All these types of pain are different from lightning crotch, which refers to the sharp, electric pains you might feel for a few seconds in your nether regions.",
        "text_sha256": "90615c41e717a4515d097ca6efd1b072076241de95fe82d2baf27ec7db225226",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When does it usually start?",
        "text_sha256": "b00967a0cf3c7a52573241b82b43b28abb6b1f3184cb27956e378482c4d5f1cd",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Lightning crotch can occur at any time in pregnancy, but it's most common in the third trimester when your baby is bigger and you’re getting closer to your due date.",
        "text_sha256": "d5c8cdce0289e51dd264ac63766bb2d3a62e8c7359dcd7d7746a7b21a59365d6",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When does it typically end?",
        "text_sha256": "3175e1091211be444d6e223b330ac55631c1a89a17f6e94a4831b68be5cf49cc",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The pain will end when your pregnancy ends and your baby is born.",
        "text_sha256": "3b153091e8aad3bfa2d2e741f1bd3b0ff6b583e4d95827df8dc775036adb0d60",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What causes lightning pain when you're pregnant?",
        "text_sha256": "e6d4b3e7dcbddc318ec062fea02be9b4cd41ce065583b3473fe81a90b5a4f865",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Why do moms-to-be get lightning crotch? There’s no one definitive reason, but there are plenty of theories on its triggers.",
        "text_sha256": "1e37ae5b8ae8468391ab69a8a1f093e8f1bd888f7196b0a99457cab8d04ddc25",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It could be that your little (yet getting-bigger-every-day) baby is pressing on or kicking a nerve that runs to the cervix or its surroundings, causing those zings of pain. Or maybe the increasing pressure of baby’s head as it drops lower into your pelvis in anticipation of the big day could create those lightning bolts in your vaginal area.",
        "text_sha256": "9eace6f7f5a2a29fe333b5744796188bf0c759b6051338a30dd796b8891ee4fb",
        "word_count": 59
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Is there anything you can do to prevent lightning crotch pain?",
        "text_sha256": "013581ea3a9653fddf005c539d747355d7886dd25a356b2089f6397b0ad0e713",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Unfortunately, there’s not much you can do to prevent lightning from striking your crotch area. If you do have those electric shocks of pain, seeking relief — while not always possible to find — by changing positions or wearing a belly support band is your only option.",
        "text_sha256": "9185ec9bf90721e73bdbcdf61c62f6ce168b8f839841d9c3458f0f966beccd5a",
        "word_count": 47
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When to see the doctor",
        "text_sha256": "38cdf6184a772bba8bde29cc9d873e377579b5e74d73dec8f38b48cb76d0bf5b",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Need some reassurance about your lightning crotch pain? It’s not triggered by cervical dilation , which means there’s no reason to worry that you're going into labor. It’s also not dangerous or a sign that something’s wrong with your pregnancy or the baby. Still, it makes sense to ask your practitioner about those twinges at your next prenatal visit.",
        "text_sha256": "4c45a94effd5d2f557b9c59a043d83c0e61edaa1ee40d578f6b65874a1ba0345",
        "word_count": 59
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Remember: You can always keep track of symptoms throughout your pregnancy using the My Journal tool in the What to Expect app , plus get tips for managing other symptoms.",
        "text_sha256": "bda9aa2c69890a798641098d067ec2a50aa8ef72a9be00522d661501fee9e48c",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Definitely alert your doctor or midwife if lightning crotch lasts for more than a few seconds, or if it's accompanied by other symptoms like vaginal bleeding, fever or contractions, or if the sharp pains don’t subside.",
        "text_sha256": "38a524d2a9961d7634fe89360ea778e3236597eb22f91988a5d750f4bcce99aa",
        "word_count": 36
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here's the bottom line: Though uncomfortable and painful, lightning crotch is just another annoying pregnancy symptom that you’ll have to endure until your baby is born. Hang in there!",
        "text_sha256": "2efb4f4dbbd88584a5fce9106c797e58b311f6dc263d7704cbe10d3197f5713d",
        "word_count": 29
      }
    ],
